  '2026-09-10: SCORING DENOMINATOR IS NOT STABLE (#758, open) — the protocol signal denominator (`signalMax`, persisted as `rawMax`) is summed only from directives whose RUNTIME signalClass was bullish/bearish on that tick. A group with no directional reading contributes 0, so when every group is silent `rawMax = 0` and composite becomes `0/0 → 0` with signal HOLD: a PHANTOM ZERO persisted as if it were a reading. Real rows for spy-day-v1 alternate 80 / 90 / NULL / 0 within 12 minutes, so the stored percentage is not comparable over time and its history is meaningless as a series. Caught while explaining a Ladder card that showed a green LIVE badge beside a blank score.',
  '2026-09-10: `protocol_score_status` reports SCORING from INTENT, not evidence (#758, open) — the loop logs `17 of 17 active protocols ready for scoring` while six of them write no Score row at all (spy-speed-v1 / vix-spike-v1 / qqq-speed-v1 stopped at 07:57; cac-speed-v1 and dax-speed-v1 have NEVER written one) and it still reports `scoring  symbolsScored=1`. A protocol claiming symbolsScored > 0 but with no recent Score row should read `stalled`. This is what made a 4-hour scoring outage invisible.',
